    "q-162985": {
      "dom_id": "step-q162985",
      "name": "Question 3",
      "problem": "A thin plate $D$ with the mass density function $\\lambda (x,y)=15xy$ is enclosed between the curve $x=\\sqrt{1-{y}^{2}}$ and the $y$-axis  for $0\\le y\\le 1.$ Find the moment of the plate about the $x$-axis.",
      "worked_solution": "The moment of a lamina $D$ with the mass density function $\\lambda (x,y)$ about the $x$-axis is given by\n\n$$\n{M}_{x}={∬}_{D}y\\,\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nIn our case, $D$ is a type II plane region, as shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/multivariable/14121640/assets/98a791c71bcad80b4e8427f1b2a311e1712fdbc8697d0475b2470c8e0281e8c5.png)\n\nSo, we have \n\n$$\nD={(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le \\sqrt{1-{y}^{2}},\\,0\\le y\\le 1}\n$$\n\nand $\\lambda (x,y)=15xy.$ \n\nTherefore, the moment is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{M}_{x} & ={∬}_{D}y\\cdot 15xy\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}15x{y}^{2}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{1-{y}^{2}}}15x{y}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}15{y}^{2}[{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{1-{y}^{2}}}x\\,\\text{d}x]\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}15{y}^{2}\\cdot {[\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}]}_{x=0}^{x=\\sqrt{1-{y}^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{15{y}^{2}}{2}(1-{y}^{2})\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{15}{2}{y}^{2}-\\frac{15}{2}{y}^{4}]\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={[\\frac{5}{2}{y}^{3}-\\frac{3}{2}{y}^{5}]}_{y=0}^{y=1} \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{2}-\\frac{3}{2} \\\\  & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
