    "q-162978": {
      "dom_id": "step-q162978",
      "name": "Question 4",
      "problem": "A thin plate $D$ with the mass density function $\\lambda (x,y)=\\frac{x}{y}$ is enclosed between the lines $x=y$ and  $x=4-y$ for $1\\le y\\le 2.$ Find the moment of the plate about the $x$-axis.",
      "worked_solution": "The moment of a lamina $D$ with the mass density function $\\lambda (x,y)$ about the $x$-axis is given by\n\n$$\n{M}_{x}={∬}_{D}y\\,\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nIn our case, $D$ is a type II plane region, as shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/multivariable/14121640/assets/1e0f4ff99aecd563d03f19f5d6a2ede10610ac7117048d2c0d229dbb9c05651c.png)\n\nSo, we have \n\n$$\nD={(x,y)\\,:\\,y\\le x\\le 4-y,\\,1\\le y\\le 2}\n$$\n\nand $\\lambda (x,y)=\\frac{x}{y}.$ \n\nTherefore, the moment is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{M}_{x} & ={∬}_{D}y\\cdot \\frac{x}{y}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}x\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}{\\int }_{y}^{4-y}x\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}{[\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}]}_{x=y}^{x=4-y}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}\\frac{1}{2}[(4-y)^{2}-{y}^{2}]\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}\\frac{1}{2}(16-8y+{y}^{2}-{y}^{2})\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}8-4y\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={[8y-2{y}^{2}]}_{y=1}^{y=2} \\\\  & =(16-8)-(8-2) \\\\  & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
