    "q-162980": {
      "dom_id": "step-q162980",
      "name": "Question 5",
      "problem": "A thin plate $D$ with the mass density function $\\lambda (x,y)=\\frac{4}{{y}^{2}}$ is enclosed between the curve $y={e}^{x}$ and the line $y=e$ for $0\\le x\\le 1.$ Find the moment of the plate about the $x$-axis.",
      "worked_solution": "The moment of a lamina $D$ with the mass density function $\\lambda (x,y)$ about the $x$-axis is given by\n\n$$\n{M}_{x}={∬}_{D}y\\,\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nIn our case, $D$ is a type I plane region, as shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/multivariable/14121640/assets/268322576d74a9d63d05e06f55011796e17c2b4ea7a96f583270b5c1cbdb14fb.png)\n\nSo, we have \n\n$$\nD={(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 1,\\,{e}^{x}\\le y\\le e}\n$$\n\nand $\\lambda (x,y)=\\frac{4}{{y}^{2}}.$ \n\nTherefore, the moment is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{M}_{x} & ={∬}_{D}y\\cdot \\frac{4}{{y}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}\\frac{4}{y}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{{e}^{x}}^{e}\\frac{4}{y}\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}4[\\operatorname{ln}⁡y]_{y={e}^{x}}^{y=e}\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}4(1-x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}4-4x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={[4x-2{x}^{2}]}_{x=0}^{x=1} \\\\  & =4-2-0 \\\\  & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
