    "q-163157": {
      "dom_id": "step-q163157",
      "name": "Question 7",
      "problem": "A thin plate $D$ with the mass density function $\\lambda (x,y)=\\frac{1}{1+{y}^{2}}$ is enclosed between the line $y=\\operatorname{tan}⁡\\frac{\\pi x}{4}$ and the $x$-axis for $0\\le x\\le 1.$ Find the moment of the plate about the $y$-axis.",
      "worked_solution": "The moment of a lamina $D$ with the mass density function $\\lambda (x,y)$ about the $y$-axis is given by\n\n$$\n{M}_{y}={∬}_{D}x\\,\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nIn our case, $D$ is a type I plane region, as shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/multivariable/14121640/assets/4730100420adb07f9ac2d4e9e6a67a8a1c299ef552b25af1163909631d260495.png)\n\nSo, we have \n\n$$\nD={(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 1,\\,0\\le y\\le \\operatorname{tan}⁡\\frac{\\pi x}{4}}\n$$\n\nand $\\lambda (x,y)=\\frac{1}{1+{y}^{2}}.$ \n\nTherefore, the moment is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{M}_{y} & ={∬}_{D}x\\cdot \\frac{1}{1+{y}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{\\operatorname{tan}⁡(\\pi x/4)}x\\cdot \\frac{1}{1+{y}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}x[{\\int }_{0}^{\\operatorname{tan}⁡(\\pi x/4)}\\frac{1}{1+{y}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}y]\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}x\\cdot [\\operatorname{arctan}⁡y]_{y=0}^{y=\\operatorname{tan}⁡(\\pi x/4)}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}x(\\frac{\\pi x}{4}-0)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{\\pi {x}^{2}}{4}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={[\\frac{\\pi {x}^{3}}{12}]}_{x=0}^{x=1} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\pi }{12}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
