    "q-162982": {
      "dom_id": "step-q162982",
      "name": "Question 9",
      "problem": "A thin plate $D$ with the mass density function $\\lambda (x,y)=\\frac{1}{y}$ is enclosed between the line $x=y$ and the curve  $x=\\frac{4}{y}$  for $1\\le y\\le 2.$ Find the moment of the plate about the $y$-axis.",
      "worked_solution": "The moment of a lamina $D$ with the mass density function $\\lambda (x,y)$ about the $y$-axis is given by\n\n$$\n{M}_{y}={∬}_{D}x\\,\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nIn our case, $D$ is a type II plane region, as shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/multivariable/14121640/assets/163575c9a1adc54e1ccda5c3008e69413c44015596146bb435a528c4159abaa9.png)\n\nSo, we have \n\n$$\nD={(x,y)\\,:\\,y\\le x\\le \\frac{4}{y},\\,1\\le y\\le 2}\n$$\n\nand $\\lambda (x,y)=\\frac{1}{y}.$ \n\nTherefore, the moment is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{M}_{y} & ={∬}_{D}x\\cdot \\frac{1}{y}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}\\frac{x}{y}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}{\\int }_{y}^{4/y}\\frac{x}{y}\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}\\frac{1}{y}[{\\int }_{y}^{4/y}x\\,\\text{d}x]\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}\\frac{1}{y}{[\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}]}_{x=y}^{x=4/y}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}\\frac{1}{y}[\\frac{8}{{y}^{2}}-\\frac{{y}^{2}}{2}]\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}\\frac{8}{{y}^{3}}-\\frac{y}{2}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={[-\\frac{4}{{y}^{2}}-\\frac{{y}^{2}}{4}]}_{y=1}^{y=2} \\\\  & =[-1-1]-[-4-\\frac{1}{4}] \\\\  & =\\frac{9}{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
