    "q-39534": {
      "dom_id": "step-q39534",
      "name": "Question 10",
      "problem": "A thin plate $D$ with the mass density function $\\lambda (x,y)=4y$ is enclosed between the line $x=y$ and the $y$-axis for $1\\le y\\le 2.$ Find the moment of the plate about the $y$-axis.",
      "worked_solution": "The moment of a lamina $D$ with the mass density function $\\lambda (x,y)$ about the $y$-axis is given by\n\n$$\n{M}_{y}={∬}_{D}x\\,\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nIn our case, $D$ is a type II plane region, as shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/multivariable/14121640/assets/f8454539cbe01d45842ab03386e06bbbdca35d400d0e214563843d99cddd5a85.png)\n\nSo, we have \n\n$$\nD={(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le y,\\,1\\le y\\le 2}\n$$\n\nand $\\lambda (x,y)=4y.$ \n\nTherefore, the moment is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{M}_{y} & ={∬}_{D}x\\cdot 4y\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}4xy\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{y}4xy\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}2y[{\\int }_{0}^{y}2x\\text{d}x]\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}2y[{x}^{2}]_{x=0}^{x=y}\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}2y({y}^{2}-0)\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}2{y}^{3}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={[\\frac{{y}^{4}}{2}]}_{y=1}^{y=2} \\\\  & =8-\\frac{1}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{15}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
