    "q-163210": {
      "dom_id": "step-q163210",
      "name": "Question 15",
      "problem": "Consider the lamina that occupies the region $D={(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 1,\\,0\\le y\\le \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\frac{\\pi x}{4}}$ and has the mass density function $\\lambda (x,y)=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-{y}^{2}}}.$ Given that the mass of the lamina is $\\frac{\\pi }{8}$ units and its center of mass is located at $(\\overset{―}{x},\\overset{―}{y}),$ what is the value of $\\overset{―}{x}?$",
      "worked_solution": "The center of mass of a lamina $D$ with the mass density function $\\lambda (x,y)$ is given by \n\n$$\n(\\overset{―}{x},\\overset{―}{y})=(\\frac{{M}_{y}}{m},\\frac{{M}_{x}}{m}),\n$$\n\nwhere \n\n- $m={∬}_{D}\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A$ is the mass of the lamina,\n\n- ${M}_{x}={∬}_{D}y\\,\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A\\,$ is the moment of the lamina about the $x$-axis, and\n\n- ${M}_{y}={∬}_{D}x\\,\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A$ is the moment of the lamina about the $y$-axis.\n\nSince we require the $x$-coordinate of the center of mass, we need to compute the moment about the $y$-axis: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{M}_{y} & ={∬}_{D}x\\,\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}x\\cdot \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-{y}^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\pi x/4)}x\\cdot \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-{y}^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}x[{\\int }_{0}^{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\pi x/4)}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-{y}^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}y]\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}x\\cdot [\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡y]_{y=0}^{y=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\pi x/4)}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}x(\\frac{\\pi x}{4}-0)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{\\pi {x}^{2}}{4}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={[\\frac{\\pi {x}^{3}}{12}]}_{x=0}^{x=1} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\pi }{12}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\overset{―}{x}=\\frac{{M}_{y}}{m}=\\frac{(\\frac{\\pi }{12})}{(\\frac{\\pi }{8})}=\\frac{2}{3}.\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
