    "q-163286": {
      "dom_id": "step-q163286",
      "name": "Question 16",
      "problem": "Consider the thin plate $D$ enclosed between the curve $y={x}^{3}$ and the line $y=1$ for $0\\le x\\le 1.$ Given that the area of the plate is $\\frac{3}{4},$ find the $x$-coordinate of its centroid.",
      "worked_solution": "The centroid of a lamina $D$ with area ${A}_{D}$ is given by $({x}_{c},{y}_{c}),$ where\n\n$$\n{x}_{c}=\\frac{1}{{A}_{D}}{∬}_{D}x\\,\\,\\text{d}A,\\,{y}_{c}=\\frac{1}{{A}_{D}}{∬}_{D}y\\,\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nNotice that $D$ is a type I plane region:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/multivariable/14121640/assets/99c35aa7510a45a0df32868964f4743f44aaff3bc3d0017ee0c9f9afb90e7750.png)\n\nSo, we have \n\n$$\nD={(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 1,\\,{x}^{3}\\le y\\le 1}\n$$\n\nand ${A}_{D}=\\frac{3}{4}.$\n\nTherefore, the $x$-coordinate of the centroid is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{c} & =\\frac{1}{{A}_{D}}{∬}_{D}x\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{3}{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{{x}^{3}}^{1}x\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{3}{\\int }_{0}^{1}x{\\int }_{{x}^{3}}^{1}\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{3}{\\int }_{0}^{1}x[y]_{y={x}^{3}}^{y=1}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{3}{\\int }_{0}^{1}x(1-{x}^{3})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{3}{\\int }_{0}^{1}x-{x}^{4}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{3}{[\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}-\\frac{{x}^{5}}{5}]}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{3}(\\frac{1}{2}-\\frac{1}{5}) \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{3}\\cdot \\frac{3}{10} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
