    "q-163288": {
      "dom_id": "step-q163288",
      "name": "Question 17",
      "problem": "Consider the thin plate $D$ enclosed between the curve $y=\\sqrt{x}$ and the $x$-axis for $0\\le x\\le 4.$ Given that the area of the plate is $\\frac{16}{3},$ find the $x$-coordinate of its centroid.",
      "worked_solution": "The centroid of a lamina $D$ with area ${A}_{D}$ is given by $({x}_{c},{y}_{c}),$ where\n\n$$\n{x}_{c}=\\frac{1}{{A}_{D}}{∬}_{D}x\\,\\,\\text{d}A,\\,{y}_{c}=\\frac{1}{{A}_{D}}{∬}_{D}y\\,\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nNotice that $D$ is a type I plane region:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/multivariable/14121640/assets/951eb7592df1645f8743817809c0d4604b779de6a3112f7fcaf6aca5f214f302.png)\n\nSo, we have \n\n$$\nD={(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 4,\\,0\\le y\\le \\sqrt{x}}\n$$\n\nand ${A}_{D}=\\frac{16}{3}.$\n\nTherefore, the $x$-coordinate of the centroid is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{c} & =\\frac{1}{{A}_{D}}{∬}_{D}x\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{16}{\\int }_{0}^{4}{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{x}}x\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{16}{\\int }_{0}^{4}x{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{x}}\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{16}{\\int }_{0}^{4}x[y]_{y=0}^{y=\\sqrt{x}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{16}{\\int }_{0}^{4}x\\sqrt{x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{16}{\\int }_{0}^{4}{x}^{3/2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{16}{[\\frac{2{x}^{5/2}}{5}]}_{0}^{4} \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{16}\\cdot \\frac{64}{5} \\\\  & =\\frac{12}{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
        {
          "key": "selection",
          "type": "radio",
