    "q-163287": {
      "dom_id": "step-q163287",
      "name": "Question 18",
      "problem": "Consider the lamina that occupies the region $D={(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 1,\\,0\\le y\\le {e}^{x}}.$ Given that the area of the lamina is $e-1$ square units, find the $y$-coordinate of its centroid.",
      "worked_solution": "The centroid of a lamina $D$ with area ${A}_{D}$ is given by $({x}_{c},{y}_{c}),$ where\n\n$$\n{x}_{c}=\\frac{1}{{A}_{D}}{∬}_{D}x\\,\\,\\text{d}A,\\,{y}_{c}=\\frac{1}{{A}_{D}}{∬}_{D}y\\,\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the $y$-coordinate of the centroid is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}_{c} & =\\frac{1}{{A}_{D}}{∬}_{D}y\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{e-1}{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{{e}^{x}}y\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{e-1}{\\int }_{0}^{1}{[\\frac{{y}^{2}}{2}]}_{y=0}^{y={e}^{x}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{e-1}{\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{{e}^{2x}}{2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{e-1}{[\\frac{{e}^{2x}}{4}]}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{e-1}\\cdot \\frac{{e}^{2}-1}{4} \\\\  & =\\frac{e+1}{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
        {
          "key": "selection",
          "type": "radio",
