    "q-163285": {
      "dom_id": "step-q163285",
      "name": "Question 19",
      "problem": "Consider the thin plate $D$ enclosed between the curve $x=\\frac{1}{y}$ and the $y$-axis for $1\\le y\\le 2.$ Given that the area of the plate is $\\operatorname{ln}⁡2,$ find the $y$-coordinate of its centroid.",
      "worked_solution": "The centroid of a lamina $D$ with area ${A}_{D}$ is given by $({x}_{c},{y}_{c}),$ where\n\n$$\n{x}_{c}=\\frac{1}{{A}_{D}}{∬}_{D}x\\,\\,\\text{d}A,\\,{y}_{c}=\\frac{1}{{A}_{D}}{∬}_{D}y\\,\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nNotice that $D$ is a type II plane region:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/multivariable/14121640/assets/e9800a42aa3086abfc36a301e6771c838d5c9413b3c3f279ee1fc85096476d9a.png)\n\nSo, we have \n\n$$\nD={(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le \\frac{1}{y},\\,1\\le y\\le 2}\n$$\n\nand ${A}_{D}=\\operatorname{ln}⁡2.$\n\nTherefore, the $y$-coordinate of the centroid is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}_{c} & =\\frac{1}{{A}_{D}}{∬}_{D}y\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}{\\int }_{1}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{1/y}y\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}{\\int }_{1}^{2}y{\\int }_{0}^{1/y}\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}{\\int }_{1}^{2}y[x]_{x=0}^{x=1/y}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}{\\int }_{1}^{2}y(\\frac{1}{y}-0)\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}{\\int }_{1}^{2}1\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}[y]_{1}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}(2-1) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
