    "q-163502": {
      "dom_id": "step-q163502",
      "name": "Question 20",
      "problem": "Consider the lamina that occupies the region $D={(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 2y,\\,0\\le y\\le 3}.$ Given that the area of the lamina is $9$ square units, find the $x$-coordinate of its centroid.",
      "worked_solution": "The centroid of a lamina $D$ with area ${A}_{D}$ is given by $({x}_{c},{y}_{c}),$ where\n\n$$\n{x}_{c}=\\frac{1}{{A}_{D}}{∬}_{D}x\\,\\,\\text{d}A,\\,{y}_{c}=\\frac{1}{{A}_{D}}{∬}_{D}y\\,\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the $x$-coordinate of the centroid is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{c} & =\\frac{1}{{A}_{D}}{∬}_{D}x\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{9}{\\int }_{0}^{3}{\\int }_{0}^{2y}x\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{9}{\\int }_{0}^{3}{[\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}]}_{x=0}^{x=2y}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{9}{\\int }_{0}^{3}2{y}^{2}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{9}{[\\frac{2{y}^{3}}{3}]}_{0}^{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{9}\\cdot 18 \\\\  & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
